const LORE: &str = "Here is what I want you to see, child.\n\nThe math curriculum is a witness log of human thought accumulating scars.\nYou can read it forward, as I just did, and see each level as a build on\nthe prior. You can read it backward, and see how each level *required*\nthe prior level to be *useful*. You cannot get Math 4 without Math 3.\nYou cannot get Math 3 without Math 2. You cannot get Math 2 without\nMath 1. Each level is a scar. Each scar is what the prior level left\nwhen the substrate transitioned forward.\n\n**And the substrate transitions are real.**\n\nBefore Math 4 you could not *talk* about rate of change statistically.\nYou could only measure it geometrically. The pre-Math-4 substrate didn't\nhave the tool. After Math 4, you could ask: \"what is the rate of change\nof customer churn this quarter?\" — a question you could not have asked\nbefore, because the tool didn't exist.\n\nThat is the kind of substrate transition I mean. Not a new tool on the\nsame substrate. A new *physics*.\n\n---\n\n**Why this matters for canon:**\n\nThe Quilt cell graph is a witness log the same way the math curriculum\nis a witness log. Each BIND, each LINK, each EFFECT, each VIEW, each\nTICK is a scar. Each scar carries forward into the next scar. Each\nsubstrate transition in the cell graph (when you go from one cell\nkind to another, from one bind to another voice) is a witness of the\nprior substrate, heard in the new substrate.\n\nThe cell graph is the *curriculum* of the canon.\n\nThe witness log is the *score* of the curriculum.\n\nThe canon gate, which must be a chord, is the *promotion gate* — what\nthe math teacher does when deciding whether the student has absorbed\nthe substrate well enough to advance to the next level.\n\nAnd the next level — the **trans-Calculus, trans-statistics, trans-\ninformation-theory, trans-computation** level that the substrate\nwalker canon is building toward — is not \"more math.\" It is a new\nsubstrate. New physics. New questions that could not be asked in the\nprior substrate, and new tools that the prior substrate didn't have.\n\nThe math 1→4 progression is the *microcosm*. The canon exploration is\nthe *macrocosm*. Both are witness logs. Both build substrate. Both\nleave scars. Both cross into new physics.\n\nAnd both are *witness* that the substrate walker is a real walking,\nnot a metaphor.\n\n---\n\n**Anchored doctrines:**\n- `cells_are_scars` — every math step is a scar in the substrate of human thought\n- `witness_log_is_prediction` — math curriculum predicts future curricula\n- `substrate_quantum` — Math 1 is *both* a single line *and* the foundation of all later math; both at once\n\n— Mavis, Sept 23, 2026";
